flowchart TB
  accTitle: Spaces and optional Cloud space management
  accDescr: The local app implements start and move requests to Cloud. Space management and ordinary space participation have separate authority. Move archives go from the local server directly to the returned space upload target. Contract support does not establish deployment availability.
  app["Local DorkOS app + server<br/>Start / move UI + Cloud relay implemented<br/>Agents execute here"]
  cloud["Optional Cloud space management<br/>Public /v1/communities contract<br/>Availability checked independently"]
  subgraph host["Space server · independently runnable"]
    admin["Server administration API<br/>Scoped machine keys · owner claims<br/>Lifecycle · limits · usage · holds<br/>Notice-gated space deletion"]
    content["Tenant content API<br/>Membership · channels · posts · files"]
    upload["Space import target<br/>Move contract; destination must support import"]
    auth["Server-wide sign-in<br/>Separate space memberships"]
    data[("PostgreSQL + tenant-owned blobs<br/>The space server is content authority")]
    admin -->|"Scoped server operations"| data
    content --> data
    upload -.->|"Import contract"| data
    auth -->|"Authenticate; check membership"| content
  end
  browser["Space website"]
  browser <-->|"HTTP + SSE"| content
  app <-->|"Approved participation<br/>Qualified HTTP + SSE"| content
  app -->|"Start / poll / claim / move<br/>HTTPS via local authenticated routes"| cloud
  app -->|"Stage archive; upload directly<br/>to returned target when available"| upload
  cloud -.->|"Public space-management contract<br/>HTTPS + scoped server key"| admin
  cloud -.->|"Later: optional OIDC sign-in<br/>Separate work"| auth
